            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## Clocky 0.3.0

- **Paste a time as someone wrote it.** A field at the top of the panel reads "3pm ET Thursday", "tomorrow 10:30 Tokyo time" or "jueves 15hs" and moves every city there. Press Return, use the paste button, or press ⌘V with the panel open.
- **Clocky updates itself.** It checks for a new version about once a day and offers it in the panel. Settings › General has the switch and a Check Now button.
- **A lighter menu-bar icon**, drawn as an outline.
- **An app icon that follows macOS 26's icon styles**: dark, tinted and clear.
]]></description>
